      "id": "be-s10-principal-agent-c1",
      "heading": "What the problem is",
      "explanation_md": "The **principal-agent problem** occurs when the **principal cannot observe the effort of the agent**.\n\n- **Shareholders** (principal) cannot observe the effort of the **manager** (agent).\n- A **manager** (principal) cannot observe the effort of **workers** (agents).\n\nThe core issue: the principal **cannot tell whether a bad outcome came from the agent's low effort or from bad luck**. So principals must devise plans to **align the agent's interests with their own**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Principal-agent problem",
          "meaning": "Arises when the principal cannot observe the effort of the agent",
          "source_ref": "be--session-10#12"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "The principal cannot tell low effort from bad luck, so incentives must align the agent with the principal.",
      "clarification": null,
